```

Since guest state sync includes uids generated on host; fine. On a guest tab, the engine may also be used for its own CPU duel; uids may collide across states but not within a state. Fine.

`mk` sets `turn`? call `setTurn`.

Events formats:
- {type:'summon', side, zone:{kind:'monster'|'emz', index}, uid, cardId, special}
- {type:'set', side, zone, uid, cardId}
- {type:'spell', side, cardId, effect, target?}
- {type:'trap', side, zone, cardId, effect, target?}
- {type:'attack', side, from, to, direct, attackerAtk, damage, destroyed: [...]}
- {type:'damage', side, amount, lp}
- {type:'heal', side, amount, lp}
- {type:'destroy', side, kind, index, uid, cardId, faceDown}
- {type:'draw', side, uid, cardId, count?}
- {type:'turn', side, turn}
- {type:'phase', phase}
- {type:'result', winner, reason}
- {type:'deckout', side}
- {type:'buff', side, ...}
- {type:'special', side, ...}

For UI simplicity, events include enough.

Zone representation in actions:
- action.zone index for monster/spell.
- attack action: `{type:'attack', zoneKind:'monster'|'emz', zoneIndex, targetKind:'monster'|'emz'|'direct', targetIndex}`.

applyAction signature returns `{ok, events}`, mutates.

Let me write with internal helpers.

Potential subtlety: `endDuel` can be called multiple times; guard if winner.

Draw effects and deckout:
- If deck empty, endDuel; then further effects stop. Check after each.

`drawCards` events include `{type:'draw', side, uid, cardId}`; hand > 7 no discard.

`resolveSpell` may end duel; guards.

Trap summon check:
```js
function triggerSummonTraps(st, side, target, ev) {
